objective:
- Tech lead / staff engineer with 20+ years turning fuzzy product asks into dependable
  systems, across startups, scale-ups, and client shops. I’ve taken apart monoliths
  more than once, built the services that replace them, and carried the pager through
  the transition. I’ve led projects from concept to launch, improved system reliability,
  and mentored engineers. I move slow and fix things.
sideProject:
  name: QuizStreak
  url: https://www.quizstreak.com
  description:
  - "QuizStreak is a daily trivia game by a two-person team: my partner creates
    the questions and runs the business, and I build and run everything technical
    on SvelteKit and Supabase."
  - Past day 900 of continuous daily play, with roughly 370 weekly-active players —
    kept fast by a handful of NPM packages and hand-written CSS.
howIUseAgents:
  items:
  - title: Done is defined first.
    description: I sign off on acceptance criteria before any code gets written.
  - title: Separate hands.
    description: Planning, implementing, verifying, and reviewing are different agents
      with narrow permissions. The reviewer checks the diff against the criteria,
      not the implementer’s summary.
  - title: I hold the keys.
    description: Pushes, PRs, and anything destructive wait for my approval.
  config:
    text: My personal AI agent config
    url: https://github.com/Gipetto/opencode-config
currentWork:
- company: QuizStreak
  location: Castle Pines, CO
  url: https://www.quizstreak.com
  positions:
  - from:
      month: 10
      year: 2023
    title: Lead Developer / Co-owner
    description:
    - Build a daily trivia game on SvelteKit, Supabase, and hand-written CSS, keeping
      dependencies minimal so the app stays fast on any device.
    - Generate in-depth statistics suitable for user rankings, comparisons, and automated
      league categorization.
    - Conduct user behavior analysis and customer interviews to identify feature opportunities
      and improve engagement.
  hidden: true
- company: Wander.com
  location: Austin, TX
  remote: true
  url: https://www.wander.com
  hideUrl: true
  positions:
  - from:
      month: 12
      year: 2025
    title: Team Lead / Software Engineer IV
    description:
    - "Lead extraction of the Property domain from the monolith into a dedicated system of record, deliberately keeping search and business logic out; serving teams including booking, payments, search, and front end."
    - "Run the migration with zero downtime: dual writes, a reconciler comparing both systems around the clock, and authoritative reads cut over field by field. Issues have been limited to data consistency, resolved without large-scale recovery."
    - "Shipped a leaner listing API on the new system of record: payloads down ~80%, cached guest API median latency down 47%, uncached host-site p99 down 57% in benchmarks, with the migration’s shadow-merge hop still in the request path."
    - "Own production reliability during the parallel run: incident response, latency diagnosis, and repair of inconsistencies, including uncovering undocumented legacy behavior and encoding it as explicit contracts."
workHistory:
- company: Culture Foundry
  location: Seattle, WA
  remote: true
  url: https://www.culturefoundry.com
  hideUrl: true
  positions:
  - from:
      month: 3
      year: 2024
    to:
      month: 12
      year: 2025
    title: Software Engineer, Contractor
    description:
    - Built custom web applications and sites for clients across industries, working in
      Next.js, Python, Django, Golang, and WordPress.
    - Built responsive, accessible interfaces from design mockups in Bootstrap and
      Tailwind CSS, and extended WordPress with custom themes and plugins.
    - Partnered with project managers and clients to turn requirements into scoped technical
      plans and deliverables.
    - Implemented CI/CD pipelines for deployment and testing across WPEngine and
      client-managed hosting.
- company: Career Break
  positions:
  - description:
    - Launched a trivia game (quizstreak.com) on SvelteKit and Supabase, covering modern
      web development, game design, and statistics.
    - Learned Kubernetes by building local clusters from scratch — how they work, not
      just how to use them.
    - Stepped away after 11 years in startups to recharge and retool before returning
      to full-time work.
- company: RevOps
  location: Berkeley, CA
  remote: true
  url: https://www.revops.io
  hideUrl: true
  positions:
  - from:
      month: 4
      year: 2022
    to:
      month: 3
      year: 2023
    title: Lead Software Engineer
    description:
    - Led a small engineering team building product growth features, coordinating with
      Product, Sales, and Support on what to build and why.
    - Architected and implemented a full-stack solution for complex, dynamic pricing
      models, building the backend logic in Python and the customer-facing configuration
      interface in React and TypeScript.
    - Supervised remote contractors in finalizing a company-wide Design System, establishing
      consistent design patterns and enforcing high code quality standards across
      the front-end codebase.
    - Improved core web vitals and user experience by analyzing browser bundle composition
      and optimizing dependencies, resulting in an approximately 10% reduction in
      application build size.
- company: Twilio
  location: San Francisco, CA
  url: https://www.twilio.com
  hideUrl: true
  positions:
  - from:
      month: 7
      year: 2019
    to:
      month: 1
      year: 2022
    title: Staff Software Engineer / Tech Lead, Growth Engineering
    description:
    - Designed fault-tolerant systems that supported multiple teams in onboarding new
      members and accelerating product adoption.
    - Mentored engineers on project and task management, engineering best practices,
      problem-solving, and code quality.
    - Oversaw remote contractors and streamlined team productivity by clarifying expectations
      and task definitions.
  - from:
      month: 6
      year: 2011
    to:
      month: 7
      year: 2019
    title: Senior Software Engineer 1 & 2
    description:
    - "Worked across four product teams: Growth Engineering, Experimentation Platform,
      Phone Numbers, and Console."
    - Built a custom-built customer data platform, integrated into the experimentation
      platform, that let teams make run-time decisions about their customers based on
      live data and computed metrics.
    - Brought the company into compliance with international phone number regulations
      via a patented workflow that provisions numbers against country-specific rules.
    - Deconstructed a monolithic PHP codebase so individual teams could own their
      development lifecycles, reduce contention over core sections, and grow their own
      back-end services.
    - Drove a culture of testing as a normal part of the development lifecycle.
    - Increased adoption of technologies and tooling to improve system observability
      and drive down recovery time from errors.
  patents:
  - type: U.S. Patent
    number: 11,153,390 B2
