aiTools:
- title: Codex CLI
  usage: Primary coding agent & harness
- title: OpenCode
  usage: Primary coding agent harness for local & personal work
- title: Claude
  usage: Regular use
- title: Cursor
  usage: Team tool
- title: Adapt
  usage: Internal company assistant; org-wide knowledge search and PR review
- title: OpenRouter
  usage: Model gateway; configured agent-based PR review
- title: oMLX
  usage: Local OpenAI-compatible model server on Apple Silicon; offline inference for agents
- title: LM Studio
  usage: Local inference
- title: Kindex
  usage: Cross-agent persistent memory graph; decisions and codebase facts survive sessions
- title: Signet
  usage: Agent guardrails; permission hooks and policy rules gate destructive commands
- title: Simulacrum
  usage: Adversarial review harness; attacks ideas and plans with concrete scenarios before commitment
- title: Advocate
  usage: Six-persona review engine; parallel red-team, peer, and user-perspective findings on diffs and designs
- title: GitNexus
  usage: Code knowledge graph; impact analysis and execution-flow tracing before every edit
agentPractices:
- title: Spec-first development
  detail: AI helps write specs; agents start with few or no open questions
- title: Architect / implementer split
  detail: Engineer designs and reviews; agent implements
- title: Focused agents
  detail: Separate plan, implement, verify, and review agents with scoped permissions
- title: Acceptance criteria
  detail: Human-ratified before implementation; independent review against them
- title: Approval gates
  detail: Push, PR, and destructive actions require human approval
- title: Version-controlled agent config
  detail: Public example at github.com/Gipetto/opencode-config
- title: CLI over MCP
  detail: CLI tools preferred over MCP servers where both exist
- title: Local model evaluation
  detail: Quantization, context sizing, and dense vs MoE for coding workloads
- title: Mentoring
  detail: Established engineering habits applied to agent-assisted work
